IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-sch8-sch9-treated`

-- Part 5 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), regulations 41 to 44: the Work Capability Assessment, that is
-- when the Secretary of State may carry out the assessment, how it is carried out, what information the claimant must give, and the
-- medical examination.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHO DECIDES. Every regulation here is about the Secretary of State's powers and the claimant's position when those powers are
-- used. The Secretary of State's wishes, satisfaction and decisions are BOOLEAN inputs, never computed. What the text decides
-- is the conditions on which each power may be used and the consequences it attaches to the claimant's failures.

§ `Part 5 — Work Capability Assessment`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 41 — When an assessment may be carried out`

-- Paragraph (1): two occasions on which the Secretary of State may carry out an assessment. (a) is a fact about the claimant's
-- case; in (b) the Secretary of State "wishes to determine" something, which is the Secretary of State's own state of mind and
-- is a stated input. The power is "subject to paragraphs (1A) to (6)": regulation 41 below combines them.
-- src:803 | Work Capability Assessment
-- src:804 | 41 When an assessment may be carried out
-- src:805 | (1) The Secretary of State may carry out an assessment under this Part where—
-- src:806 | (a) it falls to be determined for the first time whether a claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant; or
-- src:807 | (b) there has been a previous determination and the Secretary of State wishes to determine whether there has been a relevant change of circumstances in relation to the claimant's physical or mental condition or whether that determination was made in ignorance of, or was based on a mistake as to, some material fact,
-- src:808 | but subject to paragraphs (1A) to (6).
@ref reg 41(1) (src:803-808)
GIVEN `it falls to be determined for the first time whether the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a previous determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State wishes to determine whether there has been a relevant change of circumstances in relation to the claimant's physical or mental condition or whether that determination was made in ignorance of, or was based on a mistake as to, some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(1) — the occasion for an assessment` `it falls to be determined for the first time whether the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant` `there has been a previous determination` `the Secretary of State wishes to determine whether there has been a relevant change of circumstances in relation to the claimant's physical or mental condition or whether that determination was made in ignorance of, or was based on a mistake as to, some material fact` MEANS
    `it falls to be determined for the first time whether the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant`
    OR (`there has been a previous determination` AND `the Secretary of State wishes to determine whether there has been a relevant change of circumstances in relation to the claimant's physical or mental condition or whether that determination was made in ignorance of, or was based on a mistake as to, some material fact`)

-- Paragraph (1A): doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or doing voluntary work, is not a relevant change of
-- circumstances. A change counts only if it relates to the claimant's physical or mental condition (paragraphs (1)(b) and (6)(b)).
-- src:809 | (1A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or doing voluntary work, is not a relevant change of circumstances.
@ref reg 41(1A) (src:809)
DECLARE `Change of circumstances` HAS
    `the change relates to the claimant's physical or mental condition`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the change consists of doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or doing voluntary work`    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 41(1A) (src:809)
GIVEN change IS A `Change of circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(1A) — a relevant change of circumstances` change MEANS
    (change's `the change relates to the claimant's physical or mental condition`)
    AND (NOT (change's `the change consists of doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or doing voluntary work`))

-- Paragraph (3): the relevant threshold is the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for
-- 16 hours a week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12. Regulation 4 of those Regulations
-- is not among the inputs and it sets several rates; which rate is meant is not said here, so the hourly rate is a stated input.
-- Regulation 6(1) rounds a calculated amount to the penny, and regulation 6(1A) would not have needed to carve out the thresholds of
-- regulations 90 and 99(6) if such thresholds were outside regulation 6(1); so the amount is rounded to the penny (fork F-41-1).
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- src:816 | (3) The relevant threshold for the purposes of paragraph (2) is the amount that a person would be paid at the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours a week , converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12.
@ref reg 41(3) (src:816)
GIVEN `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 41(3) — the relevant threshold` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` ((`the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` TIMES 16 TIMES 52) DIVIDED BY 12)

-- Paragraph (2): where the claimant has monthly earnings at or above the threshold, the Secretary of State may not carry out an
-- assessment unless (a) the claimant is entitled to one of seven disability benefits, or (b) the assessment is for reviewing a
-- previous determination of the kind listed. The disability benefits are in the core's list of benefits.
-- src:810 | (2) If the claimant has monthly earnings that are equal to or exceed the relevant threshold, the Secretary of State may not carry out an assessment under this Part unless—
-- src:811 | (a) the claimant is entitled to attendance allowance , pension age disability payment, disability living allowance , Scottish adult disability living allowance , child disability payment , adult disability payment or personal independence payment; or
-- src:812 | (b) the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination
-- src:813 | (i) that a claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity that was made on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations , or
-- src:814 | (ii) that a claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant made on the basis of an assessment under this Part,
@ref reg 41(2) (src:810-814)
DECLARE `Review of a previous determination` HAS
    `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity that was made on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant made on the basis of an assessment under this Part`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 41(2) (src:810-814)
GIVEN `entitled to` IS A LIST OF Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(2)(a) — the claimant is entitled to one of the benefits listed` `entitled to` MEANS
    any (GIVEN benefit YIELD elem benefit `entitled to`)
        (LIST `attendance allowance`, `pension age disability payment`, `disability living allowance`, `Scottish adult disability living allowance`,
              `child disability payment`, `adult disability payment`, `personal independence payment`)

@ref reg 41(2) (src:810-814)
GIVEN review IS A `Review of a previous determination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(2)(b) — the assessment is for reviewing a previous determination of the kind listed` review MEANS
    (review's `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity that was made on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations`)
    OR (review's `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant made on the basis of an assessment under this Part`)

-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
@ref reg 41(2) (src:810-814)
GIVEN `monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `entitled to` IS A LIST OF Benefit
      review IS A `Review of a previous determination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(2) — the claimant's earnings bar an assessment` `monthly earnings` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `entitled to` review MEANS
    (`monthly earnings` AT LEAST (`reg 41(3) — the relevant threshold` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`))
    AND (NOT (`reg 41(2)(a) — the claimant is entitled to one of the benefits listed` `entitled to`))
    AND (NOT (`reg 41(2)(b) — the assessment is for reviewing a previous determination of the kind listed` review))

-- The last limb of paragraph (2): where the bar applies to an assessment for determining limited capability for work and
-- work-related activity, the claimant is to be treated as not having limited capability for work, unless they are treated as
-- having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity under regulation 39(6) or 40(5).
-- The text says "limited capability for work", not "limited capability for work and work-related activity", in the consequence;
-- it is encoded as written (fork F-41-2).
-- src:815 | and, in a case where an assessment for the purposes of determining whether a claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity may not be carried out by virtue of this paragraph, the claimant is to be treated as not having limited capability for work unless they are treated as having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity by virtue of regulation 39(6) or 40(5).
@ref reg 41(2) (src:815)
GIVEN `the assessment is for the purposes of determining whether the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings bar of paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated as having limited capability for work under regulation 39(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity under regulation 40(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(2) — the claimant is treated as not having limited capability for work` `the assessment is for the purposes of determining whether the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity` `the earnings bar of paragraph (2) applies` `treated as having limited capability for work under regulation 39(6)` `treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity under regulation 40(5)` MEANS
    `the assessment is for the purposes of determining whether the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity`
    AND `the earnings bar of paragraph (2) applies`
    AND (NOT (`treated as having limited capability for work under regulation 39(6)`))
    AND (NOT (`treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity under regulation 40(5)`))

-- Paragraph (6): "relevant evidence" is evidence to suggest (a) the determination was made in ignorance of, or on a mistake as to, some
-- material fact, or (b) a relevant change of circumstances in the claimant's physical or mental condition.
-- src:825 | (6) For the purposes of paragraphs (4) and (5) “relevant evidence”, in relation to a determination, means evidence to suggest that—
-- src:826 | (a) the determination was made in ignorance of, or based on a mistake as to, some material fact, or
-- src:827 | (b) there has been a relevant change of circumstances in relation to the claimant’s physical or mental condition.
@ref reg 41(6) (src:825-827)
GIVEN `there is evidence to suggest that the determination was made in ignorance of, or based on a mistake as to, some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change that the evidence suggests` IS A MAYBE `Change of circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(6) — relevant evidence` `there is evidence to suggest that the determination was made in ignorance of, or based on a mistake as to, some material fact` `the change that the evidence suggests` MEANS
    `there is evidence to suggest that the determination was made in ignorance of, or based on a mistake as to, some material fact`
    OR `the evidence suggests a relevant change`
    WHERE
        `the evidence suggests a relevant change` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the change that the evidence suggests`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST change THEN `reg 41(1A) — a relevant change of circumstances` change

-- Paragraph (4): after a determination (a) on an assessment under this Part or Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant
-- does not have limited capability for work, or (b) on an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions
-- criteria claimant, no further assessment may be carried out unless there is relevant evidence.
-- src:817 | (4) If it has been previously determined—
-- src:818 | (a) on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work, or
-- src:819 | (b) on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant,
-- src:820 | no further assessment under this Part is to be carried out unless there is relevant evidence.
@ref reg 41(4) (src:817-820)
DECLARE `Previous determinations` HAS
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 41(4) (src:817-820)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous determinations`
      `there is relevant evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(4) — no further assessment may be carried out` previous `there is relevant evidence` MEANS
    `a determination of the kinds in (a) or (b) was made`
    AND (NOT (`there is relevant evidence`))
    WHERE
        `a determination of the kinds in (a) or (b) was made` MEANS
            (previous's `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work`)
            OR (previous's `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant`)

-- Paragraph (5): after a determination (a) that the claimant has limited capability for work and (b) on an assessment under this Part
-- that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant, no further assessment for the purposes of reviewing the
-- determination that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant may be carried out unless there is relevant evidence.
-- src:821 | (5) If it has been previously determined—
-- src:822 | (a) on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work, and
-- src:823 | (b) on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant,
-- src:824 | no further assessment under this Part for the purposes of reviewing the determination that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant is to be carried out unless there is relevant evidence.
@ref reg 41(5) (src:821-824)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous determinations`
      `the further assessment is for the purposes of reviewing the determination that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is relevant evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(5) — no further assessment for reviewing a determination that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant may be carried out` previous `the further assessment is for the purposes of reviewing the determination that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant` `there is relevant evidence` MEANS
    (previous's `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work`)
    AND (previous's `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant`)
    AND `the further assessment is for the purposes of reviewing the determination that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant`
    AND (NOT (`there is relevant evidence`))

-- Paragraph (1) read with paragraphs (1A) to (6): the Secretary of State may carry out an assessment when one of the two
-- occasions of paragraph (1) arises and none of the three bars of paragraphs (2), (4) and (5) applies.
@ref reg 41(1) and (1A) to (6) (src:805-827)
GIVEN `the occasion of paragraph (1) arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings bar of paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bar of paragraph (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bar of paragraph (5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41 — the Secretary of State may carry out an assessment` `the occasion of paragraph (1) arises` `the earnings bar of paragraph (2) applies` `the bar of paragraph (4) applies` `the bar of paragraph (5) applies` MEANS
    `the occasion of paragraph (1) arises`
    AND (NOT (`the earnings bar of paragraph (2) applies`))
    AND (NOT (`the bar of paragraph (4) applies`))
    AND (NOT (`the bar of paragraph (5) applies`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 42 — Assessment - supplementary`

-- Paragraph (2): the claimant is assessed as if fitted with or wearing any prosthesis normally fitted or worn, or wearing or using any
-- aid or appliance which is normally, or could reasonably be expected to be, worn or used.
-- src:828 | 42 Assessment - supplementary
-- src:829 | (1) The following provisions apply to an assessment under this Part.
-- src:830 | (2) The claimant is to be assessed as if the claimant were fitted with or wearing any prosthesis with which the claimant is normally fitted or normally wears or, as the case may be, wearing or using any aid or appliance which is normally, or could reasonably be expected to be, worn or used.
@ref reg 42(2) (src:828-830)
DECLARE `Prosthesis, aid or appliance` HAS
    `a prosthesis with which the claimant is normally fitted or which the claimant normally wears`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `an aid or appliance which is normally worn or used`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `an aid or appliance which could reasonably be expected to be worn or used`                    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 42(2) (src:830)
GIVEN item IS A `Prosthesis, aid or appliance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 42(2) — the claimant is assessed as if fitted with, wearing or using it` item MEANS
    (item's `a prosthesis with which the claimant is normally fitted or which the claimant normally wears`)
    OR (item's `an aid or appliance which is normally worn or used`)
    OR (item's `an aid or appliance which could reasonably be expected to be worn or used`)

-- Paragraph (3): a descriptor that applies as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a
-- specific disease, illness or disablement is treated as applying by reason of that disease, illness or disablement.
-- Regulations 39(4)(c) and 40(3) list the same treatment as a cause in their own words (for a physical, or a mental, condition);
-- this paragraph states it once for any disease, illness or disablement (fork F-42-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:831 | (3) If a descriptor applies in the case of the claimant as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific disease, illness or disablement, it is to be treated as applying by reason of the disease, illness or disablement.
@ref reg 42(3) (src:831)
GIVEN `a descriptor applies as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific disease, illness or disablement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 42(3) — the descriptor is treated as applying by reason of the disease, illness or disablement` `a descriptor applies as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific disease, illness or disablement` MEANS
    `a descriptor applies as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific disease, illness or disablement`

