§§ `Regulation 43 — Information requirement`

-- Which of the three determinations of Part 5 a request, a medical examination or a failure is about. Regulations 43(3) and 44(2) say
-- "as the case may be": the consequence attaches to whichever of the three the request or the examination was for.
-- src:832 | 43 Information requirement
-- src:833 | (1) The information required to determine whether a claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant is—
@ref reg 43(1) (src:832-833)
DECLARE `Determination in question` IS ONE OF
    `whether the claimant has limited capability for work`
    `whether the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity`
    `whether the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant`

-- Paragraph (1): the information required is (a) any information relating to the descriptors of Schedule 6 or 7 requested by the
-- Secretary of State in the form of a questionnaire, and (b) any additional information that the Secretary of State may request.
-- Paragraph (2): where the Secretary of State is satisfied that there is enough information without the questionnaire information,
-- that information is not required. The Secretary of State's satisfaction is a stated input.
-- src:834 | (a) any information relating to the descriptors specified in Schedule 6 or 7 requested by the Secretary of State in the form of a questionnaire; and
-- src:835 | (b) any additional information that may be requested by the Secretary of State.
-- src:836 | (2) But where the Secretary of State is satisfied that there is enough information to make the determination without the information mentioned in paragraph (1)(a), that information is not required.
@ref reg 43(1) and (2) (src:834-836)
GIVEN `the information relates to the descriptors specified in Schedule 6 or 7 and was requested by the Secretary of State in the form of a questionnaire` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that there is enough information to make the determination without that information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 43(1)(a) and (2) — the questionnaire information is required` `the information relates to the descriptors specified in Schedule 6 or 7 and was requested by the Secretary of State in the form of a questionnaire` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that there is enough information to make the determination without that information` MEANS
    `the information relates to the descriptors specified in Schedule 6 or 7 and was requested by the Secretary of State in the form of a questionnaire`
    AND (NOT (`the Secretary of State is satisfied that there is enough information to make the determination without that information`))

@ref reg 43(1)(b) (src:833-836)
GIVEN `the information is additional information that the Secretary of State has requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 43(1)(b) — the additional information is required` `the information is additional information that the Secretary of State has requested` MEANS
    `the information is additional information that the Secretary of State has requested`

-- Paragraph (4): the consequence of paragraph (3) does not apply unless the claimant was sent a further request at least 3 weeks
-- after the date of the first request, and at least 1 week has passed since the further request was sent. Whether the 3 weeks
-- and the week are counted by taking the difference of the two dates, or by calendar weeks, is not said; the encoding counts
-- the difference in days, 21 and 7 (fork F-43-1). "Has passed" is asked as at a date the caller gives (fork F-43-2).
-- src:837 | (3) Where a claimant fails without a good reason to comply with a request under paragraph (1), the claimant is to be treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or as not being a severe conditions criteria claimant (as the case may be).
-- src:838 | (4) But paragraph (3) does not apply unless the claimant was sent a further request to provide the information at least 3 weeks after the date of the first request and at least 1 week has passed since the further request was sent.
@ref reg 43(3) and (4) (src:837-838)
DECLARE `Requests for information` HAS
    `date of the first request`               IS A DATE
    `date on which a further request was sent`  IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref reg 43(4) (src:837-838)
GIVEN requests IS A `Requests for information`
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 43(4) — the further request has been sent in time` requests `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER requests's `date on which a further request was sent`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST further THEN
        ((Day further MINUS Day (requests's `date of the first request`)) AT LEAST 21)
        AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day further) AT LEAST 7)

-- Paragraph (3): where a claimant fails without a good reason to comply with a request under paragraph (1), the claimant is to
-- be treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or as not being a severe
-- conditions criteria claimant (as the case may be), but only if paragraph (4) is met. "Good reason" is a stated input.
-- The result is the determination the claimant is treated as failing, or NOTHING when paragraph (3) does not apply.
@ref reg 43(3) (src:837-838)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination in question`
      `the claimant failed to comply with a request under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant had a good reason for failing` IS A BOOLEAN
      requests IS A `Requests for information`
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Determination in question`
`reg 43(3) — the determination that the claimant is treated as not satisfying` determination `the claimant failed to comply with a request under paragraph (1)` `the claimant had a good reason for failing` requests `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    IF `the claimant failed to comply with a request under paragraph (1)`
       AND (NOT (`the claimant had a good reason for failing`))
       AND (`reg 43(4) — the further request has been sent in time` requests `the date as at which it is asked`)
    THEN JUST determination
    ELSE NOTHING

