§§ `Regulation 44 — Medical examinations`

-- Paragraph (1): the claimant may be called, by or on behalf of a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State, to
-- attend a medical examination, where it falls to be determined whether the claimant has limited capability for work or for
-- work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant. "Health care professional" is the core's definition.
-- src:839 | 44 Medical examinations
-- src:840 | (1) Where it falls to be determined whether a claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant, the claimant may be called by or on behalf of a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State to attend a medical examination.
@ref reg 44(1) (src:839-840)
GIVEN practitioner IS A Practitioner
      `the practitioner is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it falls to be determined whether the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 44(1) — the claimant may be called to attend a medical examination` practitioner `the practitioner is approved by the Secretary of State` `it falls to be determined whether the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant` MEANS
    `it falls to be determined whether the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or is a severe conditions criteria claimant`
    AND (`reg 2 — health care professional` practitioner)
    AND `the practitioner is approved by the Secretary of State`

-- Paragraph (3): paragraph (2) does not apply unless (a) notice of the date, time and place of the examination was given to the
-- claimant at least 7 days in advance, or (b) notice was given less than 7 days in advance and the claimant agreed to accept it.
-- The 7 days are counted as the difference between the date the notice was given and the date of the examination (fork F-44-1).
-- src:841 | (2) Where a claimant who is called by or on behalf of such a health care professional to attend a medical examination in person, by telephone or by video fails without a good reason to attend or submit to the examination, the claimant is to be treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity or as not being a severe conditions criteria claimant (as the case may be).
-- src:842 | (3) But paragraph (2) does not apply unless—
-- src:843 | (a) notice of the date, time and place of the examination was given to the claimant at least 7 days in advance; or
-- src:844 | (b) notice was given less than 7 days in advance and the claimant agreed to accept it.
@ref reg 44(2) and (3) (src:841-844)
DECLARE `Notice of a medical examination` HAS
    `date on which the notice was given`                                              IS A DATE
    `date of the examination`                                                         IS A DATE
    `the notice gave the date, time and place of the examination`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant agreed to accept less than 7 days' notice`                          IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 44(3) (src:841-844)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of a medical examination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 44(3) — the notice was in time` notice MEANS
    (notice's `the notice gave the date, time and place of the examination`)
    AND (`at least 7 days in advance` OR `less than 7 days in advance and accepted`)
    WHERE
        `at least 7 days in advance` MEANS
            (Day (notice's `date of the examination`) MINUS Day (notice's `date on which the notice was given`)) AT LEAST 7
        `less than 7 days in advance and accepted` MEANS
            ((Day (notice's `date of the examination`) MINUS Day (notice's `date on which the notice was given`)) LESS THAN 7)
            AND (notice's `the claimant agreed to accept less than 7 days' notice`)

-- Paragraph (2): where a claimant called to attend a medical examination in person, by telephone or by video fails without a
-- good reason to attend or submit to it, the claimant is to be treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and
-- work-related activity or as not being a severe conditions criteria claimant (as the case may be), if paragraph (3) is met.
@ref reg 44(2) (src:841-844)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination in question`
      `the claimant was called by or on behalf of such a health care professional to attend a medical examination in person, by telephone or by video` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant failed to attend or submit to the examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant had a good reason for failing` IS A BOOLEAN
      notice IS A `Notice of a medical examination`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Determination in question`
`reg 44(2) — the determination that the claimant is treated as not satisfying` determination `the claimant was called by or on behalf of such a health care professional to attend a medical examination in person, by telephone or by video` `the claimant failed to attend or submit to the examination` `the claimant had a good reason for failing` notice MEANS
    IF `the claimant was called by or on behalf of such a health care professional to attend a medical examination in person, by telephone or by video`
       AND `the claimant failed to attend or submit to the examination`
       AND (NOT (`the claimant had a good reason for failing`))
       AND (`reg 44(3) — the notice was in time` notice)
    THEN JUST determination
    ELSE NOTHING
